> I'm using MinGW to compile, with Windows 8 x64. 

My first thought is that it would be a 64-bit safety error; AFAIR,
NetHack 3.4.3 doesn't compile correctly on 64-bit systems. There's a
64-bit safety patch on Bilious: <http://bilious.alt.org/?327>.

However, after reading the patch, that might well not be your problem
after all. None of the changes in that patch should have an effect on
makedefs.

If you could get a backtrace of the crash, that would help a lot while
debugging. However, I don't know how to produce backtraces for
mingw-compiled files (and a quick web search didn't turn up anything
that wouldn't be obnoxious to use). If you have the ability to run
makedefs under a debugger, do so (it should hint at what's going wrong),
but that may be far from easy.

